#Version 3
#Start-Script 
.\INT. DINER - NIGHT
..Rain streaks the windows. A neon sign buzzes, half of its letters dead.
..MAGGIE (50s) wipes down the counter.
..
._MAGGIE
.:We're closed.
._DETECTIVE HALE
..He shakes the rain off his coat and sits down anyway.
.:Coffee. Black.
._MAGGIE
.(()
.:Fine.
.((beat)
.:One cup, then you're gone.
..Hale studies the room: the cracked vinyl booths, the pie case with one slice of something that used to be lemon meringue, the clock above the kitchen door that has said ten past four for as long as anyone can remember.
..Maggie pours the coffee without looking at him. Her hands are steady, but she keeps her back to the window, and every time headlights sweep across the glass her eyes flick up to the mirror behind the register.
..Outside, a delivery truck rolls past slowly, too slowly, its driver a shadow behind a fogged windshield. It turns the corner and is gone, but the sound of its engine lingers for a long moment before the rain swallows it.
..Hale takes a sip, sets the cup down, and lines it up precisely with the edge of the napkin. He takes a photograph from his coat pocket and lays it face down on the counter between them.
..Maggie glances at the photograph but doesn't touch it. She goes back to wiping a counter that is already clean, working the rag in slow circles over the same spot until the vinyl squeaks.
..Hale studies the room: the cracked vinyl booths, the pie case with one slice of something that used to be lemon meringue, the clock above the kitchen door that has said ten past four for as long as anyone can remember.
